WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:11.510
As requirements for job applications are getting increasingly higher, college students ought to be better prepared for their future career.
随着求职要求越来越高，大学生应该为未来的职业做好更充分的准备。

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:21.890
Employers today expect not only good academic records but also practical experience, teamwork skills and the ability to adapt quickly to new situations.
如今的雇主不仅希望求职者有良好的学习成绩，还希望他们具备实践经验、团队合作能力以及快速适应新环境的能力。

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.570
To meet these expectations, students should start planning early.
为了达到这些期望，学生应该尽早开始规划。

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.920
In their first year, they can explore their interests and set clear career goals.
在大一，他们可以探索自己的兴趣，确立明确的职业目标。

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:41.600
After that, they should build relevant skills step by step, for example by doing internships or joining research projects related to their major.
此后，他们应该逐步培养相关技能，例如去实习，或参加与本专业相关的科研项目。

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:50.480
Equally important are soft skills such as communication and problem-solving, which can be developed through club activities and volunteer work.
同样重要的是沟通能力和解决问题能力等软技能，它们可以通过社团活动和志愿工作来培养。

00:00:51.280 --> 00:01:02.530
A classmate of mine who wanted to work in marketing spent two summers interning at local companies, and this experience helped her stand out among many applicants and secure the job she had hoped for.
我的一位同学想从事市场营销工作，她用两个暑假在当地公司实习，这段经历帮助她从众多求职者中脱颖而出，得到了她一直期盼的工作。

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:09.710
In addition, students should keep an eye on changes in the job market and update their knowledge accordingly.
此外，学生应该关注就业市场的变化，并相应地更新自己的知识。

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:17.970
Career preparation is not a last-minute task before graduation but a process that spans all four years of college.
职业准备不是毕业前临时抱佛脚的任务，而是一个贯穿大学四年的过程。

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:23.020
Those who prepare early and steadily will be ready when opportunities arrive.
那些尽早、稳步做准备的人，在机会到来时就会有所准备。
